WEBVTT

00:45.128 --> 00:48.006
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

00:54.805 --> 00:56.473
SEONGJAE'S TABLE HOME-STYLE MEALS

00:56.557 --> 00:59.017
SEONGJAE'S TABLE

01:01.645 --> 01:03.105
Dad, I'm back.

01:03.897 --> 01:05.274
Seong-jae, welcome back.

01:06.191 --> 01:07.192
Yeah.

01:10.237 --> 01:11.613
What's that smell?

01:15.450 --> 01:16.493
Gosh.

01:16.577 --> 01:18.537
Are you making seaweed soup
for my birthday?

01:19.246 --> 01:20.539
It's not for you. Don't think about it.

01:21.373 --> 01:22.958
What? Then who's it for?

01:23.041 --> 01:24.209
Who else could it be?

01:24.293 --> 01:25.794
It's for the one who went through so much
to give birth to you.

01:26.670 --> 01:28.255
Seong-jae, look at this.

01:28.338 --> 01:29.673
It's nice and plump, right?

01:30.799 --> 01:33.135
Dad, you still love Mom that much?

01:33.969 --> 01:35.637
You know what I think about
when I'm cooking?

01:36.138 --> 01:39.641
I think, "I have to make this
perfect for my Su-yeon."

01:39.808 --> 01:41.685
- That's what I always think.
- Jeez.

01:41.768 --> 01:42.811
I feel so left out.

01:43.478 --> 01:45.105
So I guess I have to buy my own soup.

01:45.188 --> 01:47.107
Do you want the recipe?

01:47.190 --> 01:49.610
No, it's fine. I can't cook.

01:50.485 --> 01:52.529
I'm no good at cooking,
and I don't enjoy it.

01:52.613 --> 01:55.324
You need to know how to make this

01:55.407 --> 01:57.409
for your future girlfriend's love.

01:57.743 --> 01:59.786
When you're making this
sea urchin seaweed soup

01:59.870 --> 02:01.038
do you know what the secret ingredient is?

02:03.540 --> 02:05.751
Isn't it just about
using fresh sea urchin?

02:05.834 --> 02:07.419
No, no.

02:09.046 --> 02:10.255
It's this. This right here.

02:11.006 --> 02:13.383
Once this goes into the
sea urchin seaweed soup

02:13.467 --> 02:15.135
the soup just...

02:15.427 --> 02:17.471
it's just absolutely...

02:17.554 --> 02:19.765
to die for, you know? To die for.

02:22.809 --> 02:23.894
Battalion Commander!

02:27.564 --> 02:30.025
- Battalion Commander!
- Battalion Commander!

02:36.865 --> 02:39.284
EPISODE 2

02:39.743 --> 02:41.411
Battalion Commander, you can't leave us!

02:41.703 --> 02:43.080
Our country still needs you, sir!

02:43.163 --> 02:44.164
Those sons of bitches.

02:44.247 --> 02:45.874
What the hell did they put in the soup?

02:45.957 --> 02:47.167
Get him to the Medical Unit, now!

02:48.335 --> 02:49.503
Quiet!

02:51.838 --> 02:52.839
Go...

02:54.966 --> 02:55.967
Go...

02:56.051 --> 02:57.928
I'll go tell your wife you love her.

03:01.306 --> 03:02.683
Go to a civilian hospital.

03:03.975 --> 03:04.976
Not the Medical Unit.

03:05.060 --> 03:07.062
Go to the nearest civilian hospital. Now!

03:07.145 --> 03:08.647
- Civilian Hospital!
- Hurry!

03:08.730 --> 03:09.981
Hurry, hurry!

03:10.774 --> 03:12.943
- What's going on?
- The Battalion Commander collapsed, sir.

03:13.026 --> 03:14.152
Why, all of a sudden?

03:14.236 --> 03:15.612
GANGLIM OUTPOST
(2965TH UNIT, 4TH COMPANY)

03:18.824 --> 03:21.159
I heard that after the seaweed soup
made by the new cook

03:21.243 --> 03:23.120
he suddenly had trouble breathing.

03:23.620 --> 03:26.206
In this case, under military law,
is it assault on a superior?

03:26.289 --> 03:28.041
Or the crime of providing harmful food?

03:28.125 --> 03:29.751
Damn it.

03:36.049 --> 03:37.342
A LOYAL BROTHERHOOD
THAT PROTECTS THE NATION

03:38.468 --> 03:39.678
Your military career is
totally screwed now, huh?

03:41.179 --> 03:42.222
MILITARY POLICE

03:43.849 --> 03:46.059
I'm not involved in the seaweed soup.

03:46.143 --> 03:47.269
I'm innocent.

03:47.352 --> 03:49.104
Hey, Kang Seong-jae, say something!

03:49.187 --> 03:50.981
This must be a misunderstanding.

03:51.273 --> 03:52.524
This... this can't be right.

03:52.607 --> 03:53.900
But he said if I made it this way

03:53.984 --> 03:55.277
it would be killer.

03:59.865 --> 04:02.159
I knew his food would
get him in trouble one of these days.

04:05.162 --> 04:06.538
Oh my goodness.

04:06.621 --> 04:08.915
Oh my. What in the world
is happening here?

04:08.999 --> 04:11.168
Seriously, did they put something
in his food?

04:11.543 --> 04:14.755
I should've known it when he said,
"This has to go in the soup."

04:14.838 --> 04:17.174
So he did put something in it!

04:17.382 --> 04:19.009
But it really wasn't anything special.

04:19.092 --> 04:21.344
My God, what did you
put in there, you brat!

04:30.562 --> 04:32.189
Battalion Commander.

04:32.272 --> 04:33.273
Don't worry, sir.

04:33.356 --> 04:34.566
We brought you to a civilian hospital

04:34.649 --> 04:36.359
not the Med Unit, as you asked.

04:36.443 --> 04:37.444
Are you all right, sir?

04:37.819 --> 04:40.071
We were so worried something terrible
had happened to you.

04:44.868 --> 04:46.578
I went to heaven.

04:47.788 --> 04:49.664
Sir, what are you talking about?

04:50.832 --> 04:52.584
You must live a long, healthy life, sir.

04:54.336 --> 04:56.171
I met an angel...

04:59.674 --> 05:01.218
and floated on clouds.

05:01.301 --> 05:03.053
Can you believe that?

05:07.766 --> 05:09.851
- Nurse!
- Someone's dying over here!

05:09.935 --> 05:10.936
Nurse!

05:11.019 --> 05:12.312
- Hurry!
- Hurry!

05:32.165 --> 05:35.794
The fantastic combination
of seaweed and sea urchin roe.

05:37.045 --> 05:39.589
This must be heaven.

05:39.673 --> 05:40.674
Of course...

05:41.132 --> 05:43.552
that was before those guys showed up.

06:24.467 --> 06:25.468
Wait a minute.

06:25.677 --> 06:26.678
This is so good.

06:27.220 --> 06:28.221
You really think so?

06:28.972 --> 06:29.973
What a relief.

06:30.223 --> 06:31.224
Thank you.

06:44.237 --> 06:45.238
What's this?

06:45.947 --> 06:47.032
It's perilla seed powder.

06:53.997 --> 06:56.207
It's asphyxiation due to
anaphylactic shock

06:56.291 --> 06:58.043
from the perilla seed powder.

07:04.466 --> 07:05.592
Battalion Commander!

07:06.301 --> 07:07.761
Battalion Commander.

07:08.136 --> 07:09.888
He had some trouble breathing

07:09.971 --> 07:11.431
from a perilla seed powder allergy

07:11.514 --> 07:13.099
and briefly fainted.

07:13.183 --> 07:14.893
I gave him allergy medication,
so he just needs to take it.

07:19.898 --> 07:22.442
You didn't know the Battalion Commander
avoids perilla seed powders

07:23.151 --> 07:24.152
because of his allergy?

07:25.987 --> 07:27.155
I'm sorry, Battalion Commander.

07:27.614 --> 07:28.949
I should have paid closer attention

07:29.032 --> 07:30.408
but I was careless.

07:30.742 --> 07:32.160
I will make sure to retrain

07:32.243 --> 07:33.828
the Outpost Commander and cooks.

07:33.912 --> 07:34.913
Seok-ho.

07:35.580 --> 07:36.581
Yes, Battalion Commander.

07:36.665 --> 07:38.416
Go easy on Ye-rin

07:38.875 --> 07:40.085
and the soldiers.

07:40.418 --> 07:42.796
If we just let this go,
how do we know it won't happen again?

07:43.088 --> 07:44.339
We need to teach them a serious lesson.

07:51.221 --> 07:52.472
We're...

07:53.181 --> 07:54.432
officers, after all.

07:57.769 --> 07:58.937
Straighten up!

07:59.980 --> 08:01.982
Do you have any idea
what you've just done?

08:02.190 --> 08:04.818
You should be treating cooking
like it's actual combat!

08:05.026 --> 08:06.861
Deputy Outpost Commander, that's enough.

08:07.779 --> 08:10.532
Yelling at them won't help
the Battalion Commander get better.

08:10.615 --> 08:11.616
Commander.

08:11.700 --> 08:14.202
If we let this slide,
unit discipline will break down.

08:14.452 --> 08:18.039
The sergeant takes off for a break
before meal service is even over.

08:18.123 --> 08:20.458
And the private cooks with
whatever civilian ingredients he wants.

08:20.542 --> 08:22.210
I get what you're saying...

08:24.045 --> 08:25.213
but I was there...

08:25.296 --> 08:27.799
watching him cook the soup,
so it's my fault too.

08:28.842 --> 08:29.843
Ma'am?

08:30.510 --> 08:32.137
So if you want to blame someone, blame me.

08:35.849 --> 08:36.850
On your feet, both of you.

08:37.350 --> 08:38.435
- Up!
- Up!

08:38.893 --> 08:40.562
It had to be Battalion Commander...

08:41.271 --> 08:43.023
- This weakens military strength...
- Hero.

08:43.732 --> 08:45.775
You have successfully completed the quest.

08:46.067 --> 08:48.028
With your new level,
you can use a new recipe

08:48.111 --> 08:50.697
and check favorability.

08:50.780 --> 08:53.575
SKILLS: ORGANIZE INGREDIENTS
CHEF'S EYE, CHECK FAVORABILITY

08:53.658 --> 08:55.201
CHECK FAVORABILITY

08:59.080 --> 09:00.623
DISLIKE LEVEL 40%

09:00.707 --> 09:03.418
Morale here is already rock bottom,
and you had to add fuel to the fire?

09:05.754 --> 09:08.339
DISLIKE LEVEL 60%

09:09.382 --> 09:11.301
Hey, Kang Seong-jae.
Are you looking at something?

09:12.010 --> 09:13.678
Private Kang Seong-jae. No, sir!

09:16.014 --> 09:17.015
Salute.

09:17.348 --> 09:19.934
Yes, Company Commander.
Should we court-martial them?

09:21.478 --> 09:22.479
Sir?

09:22.562 --> 09:24.022
CONFIDENTIAL PERSONNEL RECORDS

09:27.192 --> 09:28.902
I'm very disappointed.

09:29.611 --> 09:31.154
You are cooks.

09:31.237 --> 09:33.406
How can you be so careless
with the ingredients?

09:33.490 --> 09:35.617
Especially when you're cooking
for the Battalion Commander?

09:38.369 --> 09:39.496
DISLIKE LEVEL 50%

09:40.705 --> 09:41.706
Private Kang Seong-jae.

09:42.332 --> 09:43.374
Private Kang Seong-jae!

09:43.458 --> 09:44.876
Private Kang Seong-jae.

09:44.959 --> 09:48.588
Did you make soup with sea urchin roe
and perilla seed powder?

09:48.671 --> 09:50.423
- Yes, sir.
- Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

09:50.507 --> 09:52.258
- Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.
- Are you authorized to cook

09:52.342 --> 09:53.843
with non-issued ingredients?

09:54.719 --> 09:56.262
- No, sir.
- Exactly.

09:57.388 --> 09:58.389
So...

09:58.973 --> 10:01.518
where the hell
did the sea urchin roe come from?

10:07.899 --> 10:09.859
It's domestic, I believe.

10:17.325 --> 10:18.368
Did I...

10:19.661 --> 10:21.121
Did I ask you where it was sourced from?

10:23.123 --> 10:24.207
I believe the Master Sergeant...

10:24.707 --> 10:25.959
put it in there.

10:26.042 --> 10:27.043
BREAKFAST, LUNCH, AND DINNER

10:30.004 --> 10:32.090
You can't just put anything in here.

10:32.173 --> 10:33.174
Come on, sir.

10:33.842 --> 10:34.884
What was that?

10:35.885 --> 10:36.886
What do you call it

10:36.970 --> 10:37.971
when a sea urchin lays eggs?

10:38.263 --> 10:39.848
Sea urchin roe.

10:40.807 --> 10:42.934
Oh, for crying out loud.

10:43.017 --> 10:44.811
This isn't your personal fridge.

10:44.894 --> 10:45.979
What was he thinking?

10:46.980 --> 10:48.523
- Get rid of all of it.
- Yes, sir.

10:50.066 --> 10:51.860
Fortunately, our Battalion Commander said

10:52.694 --> 10:54.529
he'd be lenient with you.

10:55.864 --> 10:56.865
But.

10:58.158 --> 11:00.034
If something like this happens again

11:00.618 --> 11:01.744
I, Hwang Seok-ho...

11:02.787 --> 11:04.122
will show no mercy.

11:06.374 --> 11:07.625
- Dismissed.
- Attention.

11:08.293 --> 11:10.003
Salute. Sir!

11:11.379 --> 11:12.589
- At ease.
- At ease.

11:36.988 --> 11:38.031
Communications Security.

11:38.114 --> 11:39.199
This is Hwang Seok-ho.

11:40.658 --> 11:42.827
Could I see Kang Seong-jae's file again?

11:55.131 --> 11:56.132
Hey.

11:56.466 --> 11:58.176
- Hey, Kang Seong-jae.
- Private Kang Seong-jae.

11:58.259 --> 12:00.094
Didn't I tell you to just stay put?

12:01.095 --> 12:02.096
I'm sorry, sir.

12:02.180 --> 12:03.181
Sea urchin roe

12:03.389 --> 12:04.390
and perilla seed powder?

12:04.474 --> 12:05.934
You punk.

12:07.268 --> 12:08.895
This isn't a joke.

12:12.148 --> 12:14.525
Communications Security.
This is Cook, Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

12:14.692 --> 12:17.946
- This is Private First Class Tak Mun-ik.
- Yeah? What is it?

12:18.029 --> 12:20.406
The Company Commander says
he'll take the new recruit on patrol.

12:20.490 --> 12:23.117
Now? Then do I have to clean up alone?

12:23.201 --> 12:24.202
Master Sergeant.

12:24.285 --> 12:26.579
Sergeant Yoon asks if he must clean alone.

12:27.038 --> 12:28.623
Of course, he can clean by himself.

12:28.706 --> 12:29.874
What, I'm supposed to help him?

12:29.958 --> 12:31.084
Hey, Yoon Dong-hyun!

12:31.167 --> 12:32.835
Who told you to ditch your junior

12:32.919 --> 12:34.420
and go sleep in the barracks?

12:35.255 --> 12:37.757
How many times did I tell you
to be careful with Kang Seong-jae?

12:39.926 --> 12:40.969
DISLIKE LEVEL 40%

12:42.345 --> 12:46.849
DISLIKE LEVEL 70%

12:50.019 --> 12:51.229
Private Kang Seong-jae.

12:51.312 --> 12:52.313
Private Kang Seong-jae.

12:53.147 --> 12:55.566
Do you know why they call this
the Stairway to Heaven?

12:56.276 --> 12:57.652
Because one wrong move,
and you could end up in heaven.

12:58.069 --> 12:59.362
So you'd better be careful.

12:59.445 --> 13:01.155
All right, let's go to heaven.

13:02.156 --> 13:03.157
Yes, sir.

13:25.346 --> 13:27.056
- Private Kang Seong-jae.
- Private Kang Seong-jae.

13:27.140 --> 13:28.725
How are you finding it since getting
assigned to your unit?

13:28.850 --> 13:30.184
- It's tough, isn't it?
- Not at all, sir.

13:30.351 --> 13:32.645
No, your Company Commander
knows everything.

13:32.812 --> 13:34.063
You don't have to lie.

13:34.147 --> 13:35.148
I'm fine, sir.

13:35.231 --> 13:36.482
My superiors and the Outpost Commander

13:36.566 --> 13:38.151
- are good to me.
- No.

13:38.234 --> 13:39.402
There's no way you're fine.

13:39.652 --> 13:40.820
You enlisted only two months

13:40.903 --> 13:41.988
after losing your father.

13:42.280 --> 13:44.490
I know you're just pretending to be fine.

13:44.574 --> 13:47.410
No, sir. I'm thinking of
my mother and sister at home

13:47.493 --> 13:48.745
and I want to excel in my military life.

13:48.828 --> 13:49.829
"Unbreakable spirit."

13:49.912 --> 13:51.414
You know the saying

13:51.497 --> 13:52.999
"What's important
is an unbreakable spirit"?

13:53.082 --> 13:55.752
Well, I, Hwang Seok-ho,
can't agree with that.

13:56.627 --> 13:58.046
If you push yourself too hard

13:58.129 --> 13:59.130
you're bound to break.

13:59.213 --> 14:02.300
And I don't want to see you break,
Private Kang Seong-jae.

14:13.770 --> 14:15.730
I've warned you several times, haven't I?

14:16.064 --> 14:18.232
Do not leave your personal food
in the mess hall.

14:18.316 --> 14:19.776
Well, you know, with sea urchin

14:19.859 --> 14:21.319
freshness is everything.

14:21.402 --> 14:22.904
You trying to keep them fresh

14:22.987 --> 14:24.739
almost got the Battalion Commander
in serious trouble.

14:24.822 --> 14:27.408
Hey, let's get our facts straight here.

14:27.658 --> 14:29.243
The mess wasn't the sea urchin roe.

14:29.327 --> 14:31.204
It was the perilla seed powder, right?

14:31.287 --> 14:33.039
And that was the new recruit

14:33.122 --> 14:34.415
acting on his own.

14:35.375 --> 14:36.667
Exactly. See?

14:36.751 --> 14:37.752
PERSONNEL RECORD CARD

14:37.835 --> 14:39.879
Assigning Kang Seong-jae
to the mess hall was the issue too.

14:40.171 --> 14:41.672
Well, to be honest

14:41.756 --> 14:44.092
I told you it was risky
to make him a cook.

14:44.175 --> 14:47.428
But you're the one who sent him,
talking about high risk.

14:47.512 --> 14:48.971
I know. I know.

14:49.055 --> 14:51.432
And that damn high risk
is going to get us all killed.

14:52.308 --> 14:55.019
Look, the Battalion Commander
might say he's fine

14:55.103 --> 14:56.437
but if this keeps up...

14:56.938 --> 14:58.898
we'll all end up on his bad side.

15:02.485 --> 15:04.237
Let's transfer Kang Seong-jae.

15:06.447 --> 15:08.032
Where can we transfer him at this point?

15:09.992 --> 15:10.993
To the TOD.

15:14.956 --> 15:15.957
Have you...

15:16.207 --> 15:17.583
heard of the TOD?

15:19.752 --> 15:22.213
- I don't think so, sir.
- Thermal Observation Device.

15:22.839 --> 15:23.965
It's surveillance gear used

15:24.048 --> 15:25.883
to watch the pitch-black sea at night

15:25.967 --> 15:28.302
for any potential North Korean
submarines or vessels.

15:30.513 --> 15:33.724
It's a vital security position
for the Republic of Korea.

15:35.893 --> 15:36.894
What do you think?

15:38.563 --> 15:40.606
I believe every position is necessary

15:40.690 --> 15:42.358
for our national security, sir.

15:42.525 --> 15:43.526
That's right.

15:43.609 --> 15:45.695
In any situation,
you just have to do your duty.

15:46.112 --> 15:47.113
So I was wondering...

15:47.363 --> 15:48.573
how would you like to try

15:48.656 --> 15:50.992
a different job other than being a cook?

15:51.367 --> 15:53.703
- The TOD?
- There must be an opening, right?

15:53.786 --> 15:55.705
Well, we can make an opening
if we have to.

15:55.788 --> 15:58.207
But is transferring him
really going to make a difference?

15:58.291 --> 16:00.334
All he has to do is sit and observe.

16:00.418 --> 16:02.170
Isn't that better than the kitchen?

16:04.589 --> 16:07.467
He just put some perilla seed powder
in the seaweed soup.

16:07.550 --> 16:09.343
I don't know if that's grounds
for a transfer.

16:10.887 --> 16:13.181
I can come up with a justification.

16:14.390 --> 16:16.392
After all, I'm Company Commander
Hwang Seok-ho.

16:24.150 --> 16:26.611
But last time you said being a cook
would be a good fit for me.

16:29.155 --> 16:30.156
I did say that.

16:30.448 --> 16:32.033
But as your Company Commander,
I've been watching you

16:32.408 --> 16:35.077
and I think your talents are wasted
in the kitchen.

16:38.247 --> 16:40.541
Battalion Commander!

16:40.625 --> 16:42.418
Is this because of the seaweed soup, sir?

16:43.377 --> 16:45.588
The Battalion Commander
already settled that.

16:45.671 --> 16:46.839
Why would I bring it up?

16:46.923 --> 16:48.591
I'm just worried about you.

16:48.799 --> 16:51.844
You're up first and you leave last,
and you don't even get weekends off.

16:51.928 --> 16:53.554
I was thinking it might be too harsh

16:53.638 --> 16:56.057
for you, Private Kang Seong-jae.

16:59.727 --> 17:00.728
I'm okay, sir.

17:00.811 --> 17:02.939
- And I'm enjoying learning new things.
- All right.

17:03.314 --> 17:04.315
All right.

17:06.817 --> 17:08.736
I know exactly what you mean.

17:10.238 --> 17:12.073
Even though I'm trying to be approachable

17:12.448 --> 17:14.492
it must not have been easy for you
to open up and speak honestly.

17:14.742 --> 17:15.743
I tend to be...

17:16.285 --> 17:18.079
pretty intimidating.

17:21.040 --> 17:23.251
I've scheduled you a counseling session
with the battalion tomorrow.

17:27.213 --> 17:28.214
Hero.

17:28.673 --> 17:32.343
Complete the Class Change Quest
within 72 hours.

17:32.718 --> 17:34.470
USE THE CHEF'S EYE AT LEAST THREE TIMES

17:34.554 --> 17:36.013
SERVE MEALS AT LEAST THREE TIMES

17:36.097 --> 17:37.306
MAKE A THREE-PLUS-STAR DISH USING RECIPE

17:37.390 --> 17:38.516
Failure to do so...

17:39.141 --> 17:41.352
will cost you your opportunity

17:41.435 --> 17:42.687
to become The Legendary Chef.

17:43.145 --> 17:44.772
The Legendary Chef?

17:45.398 --> 17:48.025
QUEST TIME REMAINING

17:53.197 --> 17:54.198
Private Kang Seong-jae?

17:54.365 --> 17:56.659
- Private Kang Seong-jae.
- It's called counseling

17:57.201 --> 17:58.327
but don't be scared.

17:58.536 --> 18:00.538
It's something all new recruits go through

18:01.080 --> 18:02.540
so just relax and be honest.

18:02.915 --> 18:03.916
Yes, sir.

18:08.421 --> 18:09.964
QUEST TIME REMAINING

18:26.188 --> 18:27.481
I'm not in the military

18:27.565 --> 18:29.317
so you can just relax and talk to me.

18:29.942 --> 18:30.943
Yes, ma'am.

18:38.618 --> 18:40.077
It says here

18:40.161 --> 18:42.204
your father passed away
right before you enlisted.

18:42.496 --> 18:43.539
That must have been so hard.

18:45.583 --> 18:47.627
It's okay. I'm doing much better now.

18:48.669 --> 18:50.421
What was your father like, Seong-jae?

18:53.549 --> 18:54.550
My dad...

18:54.634 --> 18:56.594
THANK YOU TO ALL OUR CUSTOMERS
FOR SUPPORTING SEONGJAE'S TABLE

18:56.677 --> 18:57.678
Please take a look.

19:02.099 --> 19:03.100
Okay.

19:05.227 --> 19:08.022
SEONGJAE'S TABLE

19:21.577 --> 19:23.329
- Dad.
- Yeah?

19:23.412 --> 19:25.706
Dad, what are you doing
standing out in the rain?

19:28.793 --> 19:29.794
Son.

19:31.879 --> 19:33.381
I'll never give up.

19:35.049 --> 19:36.217
I have you guys and Mom.

19:36.926 --> 19:37.968
I have to see it through.

19:45.518 --> 19:46.519
My dad

19:46.602 --> 19:48.396
was the kind of person who never gave up.

19:50.106 --> 19:51.941
No matter what happened to him

19:52.066 --> 19:53.526
he would grit his teeth

19:53.943 --> 19:55.736
and endure for the sake of his family.

19:57.780 --> 20:00.408
I wonder if you have your father's
strong sense of responsibility.

20:01.826 --> 20:02.827
Well, I...

20:07.123 --> 20:08.290
So, how is military life?

20:10.960 --> 20:12.712
I think the hardest part is

20:12.795 --> 20:15.506
dealing with unexpected things.

20:16.173 --> 20:19.051
- Like suddenly becoming a cook.
- A cook?

20:20.344 --> 20:22.847
Do you think being a cook
isn't a good fit for you?

20:26.392 --> 20:29.603
THE ARMY'S TRUE TASTE
BARRACKS CAFETERIA

20:45.035 --> 20:48.581
BURN HAZARD

20:56.046 --> 20:57.131
Salute!

20:57.214 --> 20:58.340
I've returned from counseling.

20:58.549 --> 20:59.967
What did you say in counseling?

21:00.468 --> 21:02.762
"Please, get me out of Ganglim."

21:03.095 --> 21:04.096
Is that what you said?

21:05.514 --> 21:07.308
No. It wasn't that...

21:09.101 --> 21:10.936
Well, Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

21:11.270 --> 21:12.730
If you don't mind me asking

21:12.813 --> 21:14.231
how did you end up becoming a cook?

21:14.315 --> 21:16.984
What kind of question is that?
The Company Commander told me to.

21:17.318 --> 21:19.195
Besides, I figured if I learned a skill

21:19.361 --> 21:21.655
I could use it to make a living
when I get out.

21:23.616 --> 21:24.617
Private Kang Seong-jae.

21:25.618 --> 21:26.994
Oh, salute!

21:27.077 --> 21:28.662
Did your counseling go well?

21:29.663 --> 21:30.998
Yes, sir. It went well.

21:31.707 --> 21:35.169
Good. Now, think carefully about
what your Company Commander said.

21:36.253 --> 21:37.254
Yes, sir. I will.

21:38.297 --> 21:41.550
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.
I'd like some ramyun with the troops.

21:41.926 --> 21:43.719
Then when do I get to clock out?

21:43.803 --> 21:46.430
Maybe once you've done
your duties as a cook

21:46.514 --> 21:47.598
you can leave.

21:49.350 --> 21:51.769
Do you think being a cook
isn't a good fit for you?

21:52.520 --> 21:55.314
I wish I was a good cook like my dad

21:56.357 --> 21:57.942
but there's still so much I don't know.

21:58.609 --> 21:59.610
On top of that...

21:59.693 --> 22:00.694
DISLIKE LEVEL

22:00.778 --> 22:01.779
Also...

22:03.405 --> 22:04.406
DISLIKE LEVEL 50%

22:05.199 --> 22:07.076
I just feel completely lost

22:07.493 --> 22:08.994
about what to do.

22:09.203 --> 22:10.246
Don't overthink it.

22:10.538 --> 22:12.206
Just focus on handling the things
right in front of you

22:12.289 --> 22:13.582
one at a time.

22:15.000 --> 22:16.001
The things

22:16.335 --> 22:17.670
right in front of me?

22:17.837 --> 22:18.963
If you don't give up

22:19.046 --> 22:20.756
you can see it through, right?

22:22.049 --> 22:23.050
Oh, and...

22:23.759 --> 22:26.011
You know, right? Don't break the yolk.

22:29.932 --> 22:32.059
Can't they just eat some damn cup noodles?

22:34.019 --> 22:36.647
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.
Would it be okay if I make it?

22:40.025 --> 22:41.694
Just go get the ramyun from the storeroom.

22:48.659 --> 22:50.619
Don't forget to get the water ratio right.

22:52.121 --> 22:54.456
The Company Commander
wants the noodles al dente.

22:54.748 --> 22:56.709
What, are you guys single-handedly
defending South Korea?

22:56.792 --> 22:59.753
Hey, at least your work is indoors,
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

23:00.170 --> 23:01.589
We're out in the scorching sun all summer.

23:01.672 --> 23:03.757
The skin on our faces peels right off.

23:03.841 --> 23:06.886
Hey. Want to stand by this pot
like a steam sauna?

23:10.973 --> 23:12.850
What's the point of us
complaining about it?

23:13.851 --> 23:15.019
Sergeant Yoon.

23:15.102 --> 23:16.228
When's your leave?

23:16.437 --> 23:17.605
What are you talking about?

23:17.771 --> 23:19.899
I have a subordinate now,
so I can take leave.

23:21.150 --> 23:22.776
You really haven't heard anything?

23:35.915 --> 23:38.292
- Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.
- Don't talk to me.

23:41.170 --> 23:42.755
Have you completely lost your mind?

23:43.088 --> 23:45.215
- Let go of me.
- I think the eggs have gone bad.

23:45.299 --> 23:47.176
They just came in yesterday.
How could they be bad?

23:47.468 --> 23:49.261
You're not making any sense.

23:52.932 --> 23:54.266
I'm swamped.

23:54.350 --> 23:56.602
But now the eggs are giving me trouble.

24:03.692 --> 24:05.110
The eggs...

24:05.444 --> 24:08.489
All the ones that came in yesterday
have gone bad, sir.

24:08.572 --> 24:11.325
This isn't a joke.
Can you tell just by looking?

24:11.742 --> 24:12.743
What do you know?

24:22.836 --> 24:24.213
You've got to be kidding me.

24:24.296 --> 24:26.882
The Company Commander
needs an egg for his ramyun.

24:27.132 --> 24:28.217
Damn it!

24:29.551 --> 24:30.636
Seriously.

24:38.352 --> 24:41.063
This egg is seven days old.

24:41.355 --> 24:42.356
I found it.

24:42.898 --> 24:44.191
A fresh egg.

24:46.902 --> 24:47.903
Enjoy your meal.

24:49.697 --> 24:51.281
- Yoon Dong-hyun.
- Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

24:51.407 --> 24:52.408
Something on your mind?

24:53.200 --> 24:54.201
Your ramyun plating...

24:55.285 --> 24:56.453
You put some extra effort into it, huh?

25:07.881 --> 25:09.633
The egg is cooked perfectly.

25:09.800 --> 25:12.428
Your skills are getting incredible
now that you're close to discharge.

25:13.053 --> 25:15.723
I paid a little
extra attention to it, sir.

25:16.098 --> 25:17.808
- All right, let's eat.
- Thank you for the meal.

25:17.891 --> 25:19.143
Enjoy your meal.

25:23.188 --> 25:24.189
DISLIKE LEVEL 40%

25:25.274 --> 25:26.608
DISLIKE LEVEL 20%

25:35.492 --> 25:36.493
SAVE POWER

25:41.874 --> 25:43.000
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

25:43.083 --> 25:45.627
How did you end up becoming a cook?

25:45.836 --> 25:49.381
Good. Now, think carefully about
what your Company Commander said.

25:50.174 --> 25:53.052
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.
Would it be okay if I make it?

25:53.719 --> 25:55.304
Kang Seong-jae, that little punk.

25:58.682 --> 26:00.059
Plastics go with plastics

26:00.267 --> 26:01.268
and cans go with cans.

26:01.518 --> 26:03.020
Sort them into the right bins.

26:03.645 --> 26:04.980
- Got it?
- Yes, I understand.

26:06.106 --> 26:07.107
Man.

26:07.191 --> 26:09.359
I wish we could sort people like this.

26:10.235 --> 26:11.361
CLASS CHANGE QUEST

26:11.445 --> 26:12.988
USE THE CHEF'S EYE AT LEAST THREE TIMES
SERVE MEALS AT LEAST THREE TIMES

26:13.072 --> 26:14.198
MAKE A THREE-PLUS-STAR DISH USING RECIPE

26:14.281 --> 26:15.282
RAISE CAPTAIN HWANG SEOK-HO'S
LIKEABILITY ABOVE 50%

26:15.491 --> 26:16.950
Not the worthless ones
you can't even recycle...

26:17.034 --> 26:18.702
Complete the Quest.

26:18.786 --> 26:20.621
And just put all the sharp guys together.

26:25.793 --> 26:27.836
- Jeez, this guy is at it again.
- I'm sorry.

26:27.920 --> 26:29.963
Tell me what in the world
is going on in your head.

26:30.089 --> 26:32.800
Still playing the amnesia card?
Are you that out of it?

26:32.883 --> 26:34.426
- No, sir.
- You're quick with the answers.

26:35.094 --> 26:36.595
How stressful.

26:40.265 --> 26:41.308
- Salute!
- Kang Seong-jae.

26:41.391 --> 26:42.392
Private Kang Seong-jae!

26:43.519 --> 26:44.770
What's your deal, really?

26:45.479 --> 26:47.272
If you're going to act,
at least commit to it.

26:47.356 --> 26:48.816
Don't be so confusing.

26:50.526 --> 26:51.819
I'm not sure what you mean, sir.

26:51.902 --> 26:53.320
Playing dumb till the very end.

26:53.403 --> 26:54.404
Hey, you.

26:56.156 --> 26:58.867
I heard the Company Commander
told you to transfer to the TOD.

27:00.994 --> 27:03.622
The Commander's taking Kang Seong-jae
to the TOD.

27:04.331 --> 27:05.332
You didn't know, sir?

27:05.415 --> 27:06.583
Is that why you helped me?

27:06.667 --> 27:07.876
Guilty about your cushy post?

27:08.043 --> 27:09.044
It's not like that, sir.

27:09.920 --> 27:11.755
I'm not saying this
because of the leave days.

27:11.839 --> 27:14.007
It's just so frustrating. That's why.

27:14.383 --> 27:17.511
You think quitting the mess hall
for the TOD...

27:18.178 --> 27:19.179
will be easy, as he said?

27:19.263 --> 27:20.305
What are you talking about?

27:22.015 --> 27:23.016
Salute.

27:25.102 --> 27:26.103
Yes?

27:29.273 --> 27:30.274
Salute.

27:36.697 --> 27:38.115
Why didn't you tell me?

27:38.448 --> 27:39.700
What is this about all of a sudden?

27:39.783 --> 27:41.910
Did you tell Seong-jae
to quit the mess hall?

27:43.120 --> 27:44.413
From what the others are saying

27:44.496 --> 27:45.998
he's not in a good state.

27:46.707 --> 27:48.667
They say he keeps gesturing at thin air.

27:48.750 --> 27:52.296
And sometimes he flinches
as if he's seen a ghost.

27:52.671 --> 27:53.964
Every one of these things

27:54.047 --> 27:55.757
is like a warning sign.

27:56.967 --> 27:58.177
I'm his Outpost Commander.

27:58.260 --> 28:00.095
And who said you weren't?

28:00.179 --> 28:03.849
It's my call to make,
and my responsibility to bear.

28:03.932 --> 28:06.226
I just don't want to repeat
the same mistake.

28:06.310 --> 28:08.103
Would a soldier who just received
his unit assignment

28:08.187 --> 28:10.397
know about the Commander's allergies?

28:10.480 --> 28:13.275
Oh, you thought I'd just say no?

28:13.692 --> 28:17.154
I reviewed all of Kang Seong-jae's
counseling records before deciding.

28:17.237 --> 28:19.615
If you reviewed them,
you should know better than anyone.

28:19.698 --> 28:22.618
The counselor's evaluation
had this written in it.

28:22.701 --> 28:25.662
"Despite the soldier's
unfortunate family background

28:25.746 --> 28:28.081
he shows a notable enthusiasm
for military life

28:28.165 --> 28:30.918
and if given enough time to adapt
after his Unit Assignment

28:31.001 --> 28:33.545
he is expected to serve faithfully."

28:35.631 --> 28:38.884
So why are his Company Commander
and Master Sergeant complaining?

28:40.928 --> 28:42.888
Did you try the seaweed soup that day?

28:43.096 --> 28:45.974
Just as the Battalion Commander said,
it was excellent.

28:46.058 --> 28:49.144
Shouldn't you be worried
about yourself first?

28:52.648 --> 28:54.983
To be frank, at your seniority

28:55.108 --> 28:58.153
you're stuck as Outpost Commander,
a job for new second lieutenants.

28:59.821 --> 29:01.949
Even you have to admit
that's a little weird.

29:03.408 --> 29:04.910
Why are you bringing that up now?

29:05.994 --> 29:07.079
My point is...

29:09.331 --> 29:11.041
I'm telling you

29:11.541 --> 29:13.669
that you should worry about yourself.

29:20.217 --> 29:22.261
- Hey, Mom.
- Seong-jae.

29:22.511 --> 29:23.553
Is everything okay?

29:24.179 --> 29:25.681
Are you eating well?

29:26.723 --> 29:27.724
Yeah.

29:28.267 --> 29:30.435
Don't worry about me eating.

29:31.144 --> 29:32.813
I'm a cook, I'm not going to starve.

29:32.896 --> 29:34.606
Oh, that's right.

29:35.274 --> 29:38.777
You're just like your father
in that way too.

29:41.697 --> 29:42.698
What about you, Mom?

29:43.532 --> 29:44.533
Are you doing okay?

29:45.659 --> 29:47.202
Don't worry about me.

29:48.996 --> 29:49.997
How are things?

29:50.622 --> 29:52.124
Are people treating you well?

29:55.335 --> 29:57.379
Yeah, of course.

29:58.964 --> 30:01.008
Everyone's taking great care of me.

30:04.303 --> 30:05.846
That's such a relief.

30:06.305 --> 30:07.306
While I'm here

30:07.848 --> 30:09.516
I'm going to work hard and learn to cook.

30:10.309 --> 30:11.310
I mean...

30:11.518 --> 30:13.729
it'll probably be helpful
when I get out, right?

30:13.937 --> 30:16.315
I'm my father's son, after all.

30:23.822 --> 30:26.158
I thought you were still a kid.

30:27.409 --> 30:28.910
But you're all grown up now.

30:30.537 --> 30:32.122
Don't get hurt.

30:32.205 --> 30:33.206
I won't.

30:37.002 --> 30:38.503
I have to go.

30:38.587 --> 30:39.629
It's almost time for roll call.

30:40.881 --> 30:43.550
I'll be out on leave again soon.

30:44.676 --> 30:45.969
Take care until then.

30:47.429 --> 30:48.430
Okay.

30:59.858 --> 31:02.486
Would you like to acquire a new recipe?

31:04.946 --> 31:05.947
All right.

31:06.615 --> 31:07.991
Since it's come to this...

31:09.659 --> 31:11.453
let's see how far this goes.

31:13.622 --> 31:14.998
ACQUIRE NEW RECIPE?
CONFIRM

31:17.667 --> 31:19.669
Acquiring recipe.

31:25.133 --> 31:26.968
Kang Seong-jae, get back here!

31:27.052 --> 31:28.678
Yes, I'm on my way!

31:42.901 --> 31:43.902
What's this?

31:46.154 --> 31:47.155
What the hell is this?

31:49.991 --> 31:52.077
Why does the rice smell so sour?

31:52.869 --> 31:55.789
- Hey!
- The Master Sergeant wants you.

31:55.997 --> 31:58.750
So the rice stinks.

31:58.834 --> 32:00.293
Who cares.

32:00.377 --> 32:02.045
Has that bastard lost his mind?

32:02.129 --> 32:03.547
Yoon Dong-hyun!

32:03.630 --> 32:05.632
The rice smells like sour dog food!

32:05.715 --> 32:06.716
What will you do?

32:06.800 --> 32:08.718
Tell them to eat instant rice.

32:09.970 --> 32:11.638
What? Instant rice?

32:11.721 --> 32:13.723
What am I, an alchemist?

32:13.807 --> 32:16.351
You cook with smelly rice,
you get smelly rice.

32:16.518 --> 32:18.228
What's gotten into this jerk?

32:18.311 --> 32:20.355
I was lenient since you're almost out

32:20.439 --> 32:21.731
but you've gotten out of line.

32:21.815 --> 32:24.693
I can't even get discharged
until I get a replacement.

32:24.776 --> 32:26.820
What? You son of a bitch.
What did you just say?

32:26.903 --> 32:28.029
Get over here, you bastard.

32:28.113 --> 32:29.114
Get over here now!

32:29.197 --> 32:31.283
Come here. Get over here, you bastard.

32:31.408 --> 32:33.452
Hey! Come here!

32:49.176 --> 32:50.760
Three-year-old rice.

32:51.178 --> 32:52.179
D-Grade.

33:09.529 --> 33:12.616
Use vinegar to eliminate the odor
from the old rice.

33:17.829 --> 33:20.749
The sour odor from the old rice
has been eliminated with vinegar.

33:20.957 --> 33:22.209
You have gained 50 experience points

33:22.292 --> 33:23.877
and your level has increased.

33:26.713 --> 33:28.673
TODAY'S MENU

33:28.757 --> 33:30.425
Rice, bean sprout soup...

33:30.509 --> 33:31.510
BEAN SPROUT SOUP

33:32.344 --> 33:33.345
AVAILABLE RECIPE
BEAN SPROUT SOUP

33:35.180 --> 33:36.181
Hero.

33:36.431 --> 33:39.100
The bean sprout soup
is currently too salty.

33:40.268 --> 33:42.145
Add water to lower the salinity.

33:46.399 --> 33:47.609
HIGH SALINITY

33:49.903 --> 33:51.112
BEAN SPROUT SOUP

33:51.696 --> 33:54.199
EDIBLE

33:55.075 --> 33:57.702
Add Cheongyang chili peppers for some kick

33:57.786 --> 33:59.579
to earn bonus points.

33:59.663 --> 34:01.164
ADD SPICY KICK
WITH CHEONGYANG CHILI PEPPER

34:08.797 --> 34:11.550
BEAN SPROUT SOUP
EDIBLE

34:11.633 --> 34:14.469
SPICY BEAN SPROUT SOUP
REFRESHING!

34:19.683 --> 34:21.059
Hey, hey!

34:21.643 --> 34:24.854
Who said you can mess with the soup, huh?

34:25.647 --> 34:27.899
Haven't you learned
from that seaweed soup disaster?

34:29.484 --> 34:31.069
It just seemed a bit salty.

34:32.195 --> 34:34.739
Who cares if it is? What's it to you?

34:34.823 --> 34:36.866
If you're leaving the kitchen,
keep your head down till you're gone.

34:37.367 --> 34:38.702
Stay out of trouble.

34:40.245 --> 34:41.246
Yes, sir.

34:41.329 --> 34:42.330
It's hot.

34:47.794 --> 34:49.963
Jeez, that guy's a real handful.

34:51.423 --> 34:53.049
Did he do something weird to the soup?

34:58.597 --> 35:00.682
- Enjoy your meal.
- Enjoy your meal.

35:03.268 --> 35:04.811
Today's menu is boring as hell.

35:15.196 --> 35:17.115
I'm so sick of eating cereal
for breakfast.

35:17.532 --> 35:20.243
I just want a decent breakfast for once.

35:20.327 --> 35:22.621
- Hey, Kim Kwan-cheol.
- Enjoy your meal.

35:23.079 --> 35:25.665
Who said you could eat cereal?

35:25.874 --> 35:28.376
You know you can go to the stockade
for skipping meals, right?

35:28.460 --> 35:30.086
Do you think I'd be doing this
if the food was edible?

35:30.170 --> 35:31.171
What did you say, you punk?

35:31.254 --> 35:32.631
What, you think eating this

35:32.714 --> 35:34.549
is going to kill you?

35:35.675 --> 35:36.676
You little punk.

35:38.178 --> 35:39.471
You've gotten so soft.

35:40.096 --> 35:41.097
Damn.

35:42.015 --> 35:43.725
This is paid for by taxpayer money!

35:44.726 --> 35:46.936
Just shut up and eat it.

36:03.578 --> 36:05.455
Why is this so refreshing?

36:06.039 --> 36:08.166
Maybe it's because you're hungover
from last night, sir.

36:09.084 --> 36:11.169
It just clears everything up.

36:11.836 --> 36:13.838
This is the perfect hangover cure.

36:14.673 --> 36:17.425
This is something else, huh?

36:19.427 --> 36:20.428
Goodness.

36:27.602 --> 36:28.603
Damn.

36:30.271 --> 36:31.648
Hey, hey, Yoon Dong-hyun!

36:31.731 --> 36:32.941
What is it now, sir?

36:33.024 --> 36:35.318
See? You can do it when you actually try.

36:35.402 --> 36:37.737
The sour smell in the rice
is totally gone.

36:40.573 --> 36:41.574
Wait...

36:48.081 --> 36:49.499
The refreshing asparagine

36:49.582 --> 36:51.793
and Cheongyang chili pepper
create a synergy.

36:51.876 --> 36:54.796
It feels like far more of a surprise

36:54.879 --> 36:56.965
than feeling a cool AC blast

36:57.048 --> 36:59.008
from a shop on a sweltering summer day.

37:07.434 --> 37:10.019
Do these guys have a parasite
or something? What's going on?

37:10.103 --> 37:12.480
The soup is surprisingly good today, sir.

37:12.605 --> 37:13.732
Don't bullshit me, you punk.

37:13.815 --> 37:14.983
At least make it believable.

37:15.191 --> 37:18.069
There's nothing I hate more
than people messing with food.

37:18.153 --> 37:19.195
I'm serious.

37:37.505 --> 37:38.506
You okay?

37:38.590 --> 37:39.716
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol.

37:39.799 --> 37:41.259
I want to live!

37:43.970 --> 37:45.805
Let's just get through this battle...

37:46.598 --> 37:47.849
You got a death wish or something?

37:48.266 --> 37:49.726
Stay focused this time.

37:52.896 --> 37:55.106
Let's all make it out of this alive.

37:56.483 --> 37:58.234
Charge!

38:39.275 --> 38:40.985
- Master Sergeant.
- Master Sergeant?

38:43.071 --> 38:44.989
So zingy.

39:03.800 --> 39:04.843
Let's go!

39:15.562 --> 39:16.729
Now this is what I call

39:17.438 --> 39:20.859
a true victory for army food!

39:24.445 --> 39:29.367
- Bean sprout soup!
- Bean sprout soup!

39:32.620 --> 39:34.330
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol, are you okay?

39:35.415 --> 39:36.416
Yeah.

39:36.708 --> 39:37.750
I'm... I'm okay.

39:38.042 --> 39:39.043
What's going on?

39:39.252 --> 39:40.295
Why is everyone acting like this?

39:51.306 --> 39:54.684
What is this? This refreshing flavor
filling my mouth...

39:54.976 --> 39:58.605
It reminds me of a taste
from a night I struck out at a club.

39:58.980 --> 40:02.191
That's it. It's the clean flavor

40:02.275 --> 40:05.737
of a 24-hr Jeonju bean sprout soup place.

40:24.881 --> 40:28.051
LIKEABILITY 20%

40:34.474 --> 40:35.475
CLASS CHANGE QUEST:
USE THE CHEF'S EYE AT LEAST THREE TIMES

40:35.558 --> 40:36.976
SERVE MEALS AT LEAST THREE TIMES

40:37.060 --> 40:38.061
MAKE A THREE-PLUS-STAR DISH USING RECIPE

40:38.144 --> 40:39.228
RAISE CAPTAIN HWANG SEOK-HO'S
LIKEABILITY ABOVE 50%

40:39.312 --> 40:41.940
You have not completed the quest yet.

40:42.231 --> 40:44.233
Increase Captain Hwang
Seok-ho's likeability

40:44.317 --> 40:46.110
to change your class.

41:05.463 --> 41:06.714
What's going on?

41:06.798 --> 41:08.883
You'd think they haven't eaten in days.

41:08.967 --> 41:10.468
Tell me about it.

41:11.552 --> 41:12.720
Jeez...

41:15.807 --> 41:16.808
Master Sergeant.

41:17.934 --> 41:18.935
Are you all right?

41:19.519 --> 41:20.520
Are you okay?

41:23.231 --> 41:24.399
It's not just...

41:26.359 --> 41:27.360
a soup.

41:28.778 --> 41:29.862
Well, enjoy your meal.

41:29.946 --> 41:31.572
- Go on, eat.
- Yes, ma'am.

41:53.094 --> 41:56.305
I finally feel alive again.
I haven't had a proper meal in ages.

41:56.681 --> 41:57.932
I have to admit, I was surprised.

41:58.016 --> 42:00.852
Felt like we had civilian food
at the outpost in a long time.

42:00.935 --> 42:03.688
There's no way Yoon Dong-hyun
suddenly got his act together.

42:03.896 --> 42:06.149
And it's even less likely
it was all Kang Seong-jae.

42:06.232 --> 42:08.693
No, that rookie can barely
take care of himself.

42:09.235 --> 42:11.863
Right? Did Yoon Dong-hyun
really have some kind of awakening?

42:13.906 --> 42:14.907
Probably not.

42:23.583 --> 42:24.667
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

42:24.876 --> 42:26.085
I'm at my breaking point.

42:26.335 --> 42:28.254
Ever since the seaweed soup incident

42:28.337 --> 42:30.006
the Company Commander's been on edge.

42:30.089 --> 42:32.133
He's making us empty the warehouse
just to check inventory

42:32.550 --> 42:33.551
and the Master Sergeant...

42:34.427 --> 42:36.429
He's pretending he didn't
mess up the supply order.

42:39.182 --> 42:42.977
Hey, didn't the supplies that arrived
this time seem totally spoiled?

42:43.061 --> 42:46.189
Yeah, I've been hearing
a lot of complaints about that.

42:46.689 --> 42:48.316
But what's the point of talking
when nothing will change?

42:48.900 --> 42:50.860
I think it's gotten worse
since they changed suppliers.

42:50.943 --> 42:51.944
I see.

42:52.528 --> 42:54.489
I'm an idiot to expect good quality.

42:54.572 --> 42:56.157
I really am.

42:57.825 --> 42:59.660
- Private Kang Seong-jae.
- Hey.

43:08.086 --> 43:09.295
TOMATO

43:09.378 --> 43:10.797
Hey, hey!

43:11.214 --> 43:14.175
- Private Kang Seong-jae.
- Did you check that properly?

43:14.717 --> 43:16.677
If you do a sloppy job now,
you'll get hell for it later.

43:17.470 --> 43:19.138
The oxtail soup expires
June 17 of next year.

43:19.222 --> 43:20.348
We got a total of 20.

43:20.598 --> 43:21.891
The seasoned seaweed expires September 12.

43:22.016 --> 43:23.017
We got two boxes.

43:23.643 --> 43:26.104
We have to use up
the burger buns by August 30.

43:27.480 --> 43:28.564
Okay, got it.

43:28.648 --> 43:29.649
Yes, sir.

43:37.073 --> 43:38.074
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

43:38.157 --> 43:39.325
Are you going to let him transfer?

43:40.118 --> 43:42.453
You know you need a replacement
if you want to take a leave.

43:42.537 --> 43:43.996
You think I don't know that?

43:52.672 --> 43:54.382
- Outpost Commander.
- Yeah?

43:55.466 --> 43:56.884
It's about Kang Seong-jae.

43:56.968 --> 43:57.969
Can you...

43:58.052 --> 43:59.804
please let him stay in the mess hall?

44:00.138 --> 44:01.472
Hey, Yoon Dong-hyun.

44:01.556 --> 44:03.516
You're about to
ask for leave again, aren't you?

44:04.684 --> 44:06.811
I tried talking to the Company Commander.

44:08.271 --> 44:09.480
But I'm not sure.

44:10.481 --> 44:12.775
Didn't you notice that today's meal

44:12.859 --> 44:14.569
was completely different from usual?

44:15.194 --> 44:17.113
You didn't touch the seasoned spinach

44:17.196 --> 44:18.990
and braised potatoes that I made.

44:19.282 --> 44:21.617
But you scraped your bowls clean with
the bean sprout soup

44:21.701 --> 44:22.910
didn't you?

44:23.327 --> 44:24.328
What are you saying?

44:24.787 --> 44:26.831
So you didn't make the bean sprout soup?

44:26.914 --> 44:29.709
That's right. And getting rid of the
sour smell from the rice...

44:30.293 --> 44:31.794
that was all Kang Seong-jae's doing.

44:35.298 --> 44:36.299
Kang Seong-jae did?

44:37.550 --> 44:38.551
Is that right?

44:42.805 --> 44:43.890
Salute!

44:46.601 --> 44:48.561
We've got time until dinner

44:48.644 --> 44:49.645
so rest while you can.

44:50.646 --> 44:52.732
Don't feel bad leaving the kitchen.

44:53.733 --> 44:54.817
No need to put on a show.

44:56.068 --> 44:57.195
Yes, sir.

45:10.625 --> 45:11.876
By the way.

45:12.501 --> 45:15.087
What did you do to the bean sprout soup?

45:16.881 --> 45:18.716
I just added a bit more water

45:18.799 --> 45:20.218
and Cheongyang chili pepper.

45:20.468 --> 45:23.137
Right? I thought it was a big secret.

45:23.221 --> 45:25.389
Hey, if that's all it took,
I could've done that.

45:26.474 --> 45:28.726
Yes, I think everyone liked it

45:28.809 --> 45:30.102
just from that basic seasoning tweak.

45:30.186 --> 45:31.187
So you're saying...

45:31.771 --> 45:32.772
I can't season food?

45:34.106 --> 45:35.983
Everyone just has different tastes.

45:36.067 --> 45:37.443
It's not a big deal.

45:45.368 --> 45:46.369
Hey...

45:48.246 --> 45:50.414
Can't you just stay here?

46:06.055 --> 46:07.098
QUEST TIME REMAINING

46:07.181 --> 46:09.642
Complete the Class Change Quest.

46:18.985 --> 46:20.027
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

46:21.320 --> 46:22.571
Well, the thing is...

46:23.990 --> 46:25.950
I want to stay on as a cook, too.

46:30.997 --> 46:31.998
Right.

46:32.915 --> 46:34.667
The Company Commander
is impossible to reason with.

46:34.959 --> 46:36.168
So what can you do?

46:37.712 --> 46:40.423
Couldn't we just change
the Company Commander's mind?

46:40.673 --> 46:42.925
Look, he does what he says he'll do.

46:43.009 --> 46:45.136
How can you change his stubborn mind?

46:45.219 --> 46:46.595
If talking doesn't solve it

46:46.887 --> 46:48.597
there must be another way, right?

46:48.681 --> 46:50.641
GIYOUNG AND CHIKINI

46:53.561 --> 46:55.187
Why did the eggs have to go bad?

46:55.396 --> 46:57.857
Wait, are you afraid,
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun?

46:58.149 --> 46:59.150
Me?

46:59.233 --> 47:01.068
Why would I be afraid of anything?

47:01.277 --> 47:03.738
But it's so intimidating.
What should I do?

47:03.821 --> 47:05.114
What do you mean?

47:05.197 --> 47:06.907
Just go up to it and ask nicely.

47:18.085 --> 47:19.211
I'm sorry.

47:23.758 --> 47:24.759
Oh, freeze.

47:25.259 --> 47:26.344
Don't come any closer!

47:35.394 --> 47:36.729
It's piping hot.

47:36.812 --> 47:39.315
You know,
I think we might be overdoing this.

47:39.398 --> 47:40.983
I wonder if this will even
make a difference.

47:41.776 --> 47:44.612
But we don't have
any other options, do we?

47:44.695 --> 47:47.073
But of all the things you could make,
why pork cutlet?

47:48.199 --> 47:49.200
Just because.

47:49.575 --> 47:51.369
Doesn't everyone like pork cutlet?

47:52.286 --> 47:55.414
I guess so. No man in the Republic
of Korea would hate it.

47:55.623 --> 47:57.625
They say food made from the heart

47:57.917 --> 48:00.544
has the power to move people.

48:00.961 --> 48:02.963
Who on earth said that?

48:03.047 --> 48:04.382
That's ridiculous.

48:04.548 --> 48:06.092
My father used to say that.

48:06.884 --> 48:08.135
No wonder.

48:08.219 --> 48:11.347
It sounded like real words of wisdom.

48:14.558 --> 48:16.852
PORK BELLY, PORK BELLY,
PORK BELLY, PORK NECK

48:16.936 --> 48:18.437
PORK BELLY, PORK BELLY, PORK BELLY

48:18.521 --> 48:20.439
PORK NECK

48:21.732 --> 48:24.151
I don't think I can make pork cutlet
with this.

48:24.443 --> 48:25.986
I need something like tenderloin

48:26.070 --> 48:27.446
or sirloin.

48:27.530 --> 48:28.739
Can't you just work with it?

48:29.156 --> 48:31.033
It'll be a pain to get that kind of meat.

48:31.117 --> 48:34.161
It's not like
we can just go out and buy it.

48:40.251 --> 48:41.252
I got it.

48:41.752 --> 48:43.045
We have her.

48:47.550 --> 48:48.801
GANGLIM OUTPOST

48:58.310 --> 49:00.104
Smell.

49:03.065 --> 49:05.693
If the soldiers don't eat

49:05.776 --> 49:07.987
how can they defend our country, huh?

49:08.612 --> 49:10.865
- A full stomach is most important.
- Miss Jung!

49:15.035 --> 49:17.788
What's gotten into you?
Why so eager to help this old lady?

49:18.164 --> 49:21.542
Usually, you can't be bothered,
even when I call for you.

49:21.625 --> 49:23.878
Hey, don't say that.
Someone might get the wrong idea.

49:23.961 --> 49:25.171
Hey, Miss Jung.

49:25.629 --> 49:28.549
Could you possibly do me a favor?

49:32.178 --> 49:33.304
I knew it.

49:33.679 --> 49:34.680
What is it?

49:34.763 --> 49:36.515
IRONCLAD COASTAL SECURITY

49:41.604 --> 49:43.522
GRADE A PORK LOIN

49:44.482 --> 49:47.193
PROTEIN GOOD, PROTEIN GREAT,
PROTEIN GOOD, FIBER GOOD!

49:47.276 --> 49:48.277
FIBER NICE, NICE

49:48.360 --> 49:49.945
The muscle fiber is consistent

49:50.321 --> 49:52.114
and it's not overly fatty.

49:52.907 --> 49:54.283
This meat is in perfect condition.

49:54.366 --> 49:57.703
I picked through them all
to bring you the very best cut.

49:58.078 --> 49:59.788
Cuts like these are the best

49:59.872 --> 50:01.665
for locking in the juices when fried.

50:01.957 --> 50:04.752
Wow, how do you raise your pigs
to get cuts this good?

50:04.835 --> 50:08.172
What do you mean?
We feed them our leftovers.

50:08.255 --> 50:09.757
Of course they're going to turn out great.

50:11.133 --> 50:12.343
And also...

50:12.718 --> 50:14.595
Discount for soldiers available.

50:14.678 --> 50:15.679
Salute!

50:16.096 --> 50:17.097
Salute.

50:19.350 --> 50:21.185
Have you ever even made
pork cutlet before?

50:21.519 --> 50:24.230
This is actually my first time
frying anything in my entire life.

50:25.397 --> 50:27.900
Then what gave you the nerve
to say you'd make pork cutlet?

50:35.449 --> 50:37.451
Pork cutlet recipe acquired.

51:04.478 --> 51:06.605
That color looks amazing.
It's unbelievable.

51:06.855 --> 51:07.856
SEONG-JAE'S FIRST PORK CUTLET
VERY SALTY

51:08.816 --> 51:11.694
SEONG-JAE'S FIRST PORK CUTLET
VERY SALTY

51:12.278 --> 51:14.363
Wait, I think something's wrong.

51:17.741 --> 51:18.784
It's so salty.

51:18.867 --> 51:20.160
Hey, why is it so salty?

51:24.415 --> 51:25.791
SEASON THE TRIMMED MEAT
WITH FINE SALT AND PEPPER

51:25.874 --> 51:27.418
FINE SALT

51:28.460 --> 51:31.213
I was supposed to season it with fine salt

51:31.589 --> 51:33.591
but I think I accidentally
used coarse salt instead.

51:33.799 --> 51:34.967
You did that on purpose, didn't you?

51:43.058 --> 51:44.643
FRYING TEMPERATURE: OPTIMAL

51:46.312 --> 51:47.646
The frying temperature is optimal.

52:01.243 --> 52:02.328
Go!

52:21.221 --> 52:24.016
A PERFECTLY FRIED PORK CUTLET
"GOLDEN AND CRISPY"

52:24.099 --> 52:25.934
How is it, Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun?

52:26.018 --> 52:27.311
Even the Company Commander himself

52:28.228 --> 52:30.022
can't resist this flavor.

52:42.201 --> 52:43.202
All right.

52:43.285 --> 52:44.995
NEW POST

52:45.371 --> 52:46.580
Don't worry.

52:47.373 --> 52:49.708
I'll protect our country.

52:50.376 --> 52:51.377
You...

52:52.378 --> 52:53.545
just get some sleep.

52:54.129 --> 52:57.049
Rest easy.

52:57.675 --> 52:59.551
Man, this caption...

53:01.178 --> 53:02.179
Come in.

53:04.723 --> 53:06.475
- Salute!
- Oh...

53:07.017 --> 53:08.018
I was just heading

53:08.102 --> 53:10.604
to the mess hall about your reassignment.

53:11.063 --> 53:12.064
What's going on?

53:12.398 --> 53:15.234
Company Commander, I made a special
dish for you in case you were hungry.

53:17.778 --> 53:19.363
All of a sudden? For me?

53:19.697 --> 53:20.698
Why?

53:20.864 --> 53:22.449
Well, you see, sir...

53:23.534 --> 53:24.743
You think the Company Commander

53:24.827 --> 53:26.829
will be swayed by a measly pork cutlet?

53:28.080 --> 53:29.456
If it's all right with you...

53:30.249 --> 53:32.334
I'd like to remain a cook.

53:35.337 --> 53:36.588
Private Kang Seong-jae.

53:39.091 --> 53:41.301
I just don't get

53:41.510 --> 53:42.803
what's going through your head.

53:43.345 --> 53:45.013
If you taste the pork cutlet

53:45.097 --> 53:46.598
you'll understand why
I must remain a cook.

53:46.682 --> 53:47.683
Unfortunately.

53:49.184 --> 53:51.645
The thing is,
I'm not a big fan of pork cutlets.

54:07.953 --> 54:09.329
- What happened?
- The Company Commander

54:09.580 --> 54:11.373
doesn't like port cutlets.

54:12.082 --> 54:13.375
He doesn't like pork cutlets?

54:13.917 --> 54:14.918
Why?

54:15.252 --> 54:17.921
No... how on earth?

54:19.673 --> 54:21.175
- Salute!
- Hey.

54:22.342 --> 54:23.510
Seong-jae, come outside for a second.

54:23.802 --> 54:24.803
Yes, ma'am.

54:27.473 --> 54:28.474
Seriously...

54:29.767 --> 54:30.768
Damn it.

54:32.811 --> 54:35.230
You tried to give
the Company Commander cutlets?

54:35.564 --> 54:36.565
Yes, ma'am.

54:37.733 --> 54:38.776
You went to a lot of trouble.

54:39.359 --> 54:43.197
Your rank doesn't matter.
Get through military life safely.

54:48.660 --> 54:49.661
I think...

54:49.745 --> 54:50.954
I understand now.

54:54.166 --> 54:55.167
Why today...

54:56.251 --> 54:57.711
I worked so hard.

55:01.840 --> 55:03.300
I had this thought

55:03.383 --> 55:05.093
while I was making the pork cutlets.

55:09.389 --> 55:11.350
This is why food made with heart...

55:12.768 --> 55:15.395
is bound to move people.

55:17.189 --> 55:18.232
But...

55:18.690 --> 55:20.943
without even a chance to let
the Company Commander taste it

55:21.026 --> 55:22.402
it's honestly upsetting

55:24.029 --> 55:25.489
that it's just getting cold.

55:29.159 --> 55:30.661
Transfer him to TOD, effective tomorrow.

55:33.539 --> 55:35.916
- May I ask you something, sir?
- What is it?

55:36.375 --> 55:37.501
Do you believe

55:37.584 --> 55:38.794
that your own judgment

55:38.877 --> 55:41.088
is more important than a soldier's will?

55:41.964 --> 55:42.965
Ye-rin.

55:43.215 --> 55:44.591
I've got a question for you, too.

55:44.675 --> 55:48.136
What's so special about Kang Seong-jae
that you want him in the kitchen?

55:48.220 --> 55:51.640
The soldiers are more satisfied
since Seong-jae got here.

55:51.723 --> 55:54.059
That's just because Yoon Dong-hyun
is such a terrible cook.

55:54.142 --> 55:56.562
When the old rice started to smell awful

55:56.728 --> 55:58.647
I saw Private Kang Seong-jae
fix the problem.

55:58.939 --> 56:01.149
Have you tried the bean sprout soup
that Seong-jae made?

56:01.233 --> 56:03.277
The guys scraped their bowls clean.

56:03.443 --> 56:05.988
This is how
you objectively judge a soldier.

56:06.321 --> 56:07.364
Not by some documents.

56:07.656 --> 56:10.117
I try to be nice,
and you keep trying to lecture me.

56:11.368 --> 56:12.369
Hey.

56:12.452 --> 56:13.453
Cho Ye-rin.

56:14.955 --> 56:18.083
Have you already forgotten
why you were sent back to Ganglim?

56:22.671 --> 56:23.922
This probably won't mean much

56:24.131 --> 56:25.424
but could I try some?

56:28.260 --> 56:29.428
Yes, of course.

56:39.438 --> 56:41.648
I'm glad I can share some with you,
Outpost Commander.

56:42.900 --> 56:44.067
Thanks, I'll enjoy it.

56:49.364 --> 56:50.532
You know

56:50.616 --> 56:52.451
it's not my decision to make.

56:54.536 --> 56:55.537
I understand.

56:55.621 --> 56:57.873
As long as you enjoy the meal,
Outpost Commander

56:58.248 --> 57:00.375
then I feel like I've done my job.

57:05.297 --> 57:07.925
QUEST TIME REMAINING

57:08.008 --> 57:09.885
THE CHEF'S PATH HAS ENDED

57:09.968 --> 57:12.304
You have failed the Class Change Quest.

57:13.096 --> 57:15.223
Ending The Chef's Path.

57:21.146 --> 57:23.231
Even with a dish made with all my heart

57:23.315 --> 57:25.609
in the end, I couldn't change a thing.

57:28.320 --> 57:29.321
And just like that...

57:30.530 --> 57:32.616
my life of always running away

57:33.283 --> 57:34.785
hadn't changed either.

57:44.211 --> 57:50.133
EAT WELL, DEFEND TOGETHER

58:46.565 --> 58:48.942
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

58:49.026 --> 58:50.986
It's an emergency! An emergency!

58:51.069 --> 58:52.487
He's demanding to go back North.

58:52.863 --> 58:55.365
I'm telling you,
we're all dead if he goes back.

58:55.449 --> 58:58.076
Look at him, taking credit
for food he didn't make.

58:58.160 --> 58:59.161
You try it then.

58:59.786 --> 59:01.413
A congressman and a commander, now?

59:01.496 --> 59:02.748
Of all the times...

59:02.831 --> 59:04.166
It's braised boneless pollock.

59:04.249 --> 59:06.460
So you're saying
there's a problem with the meals?

59:06.543 --> 59:07.836
Private Kang Seong-jae, I apologize.

59:07.919 --> 59:09.963
Why do you think
active soldiers have voted it

59:10.047 --> 59:11.673
the worst meal every time?

59:11.882 --> 59:13.467
I can't get rid of that fishy smell

59:14.092 --> 59:15.093
you get from frozen food.

59:15.177 --> 59:17.345
Then get rid of it, no matter what!

59:17.429 --> 59:18.764
- There's no time.
- Warning.

59:18.847 --> 59:20.307
Looks like an accident happened.

59:20.724 --> 59:21.933
What did you do?
